{"nodes": [{"id": "development_plan_development_plan", "label": "TradeWatch Development Plan", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Phases are ordered by dependency, not by how interesting they are. No phase begins before its predecessor's exit criteria are all true; every phase ends with the system running; every phase adds tests at its own level. No time estimates are given because they would be invented."}, {"id": "development_plan_phase_0_foundations", "label": "Phase 0 \u2014 Foundations", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "development_plan_phase_1_vertical_slice", "label": "Phase 1 \u2014 Vertical Slice", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The most important phase: it proves the whole shape of the system with the smallest possible amount of infrastructure. Two deliberate deviations \u2014 the full schema was built rather than three tables, and bars came from the provider's historical endpoint rather than live aggregation."}, {"id": "development_plan_phase_2_kafka_backbone", "label": "Phase 2 \u2014 Kafka Backbone and Service Split", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Justified by a concrete requirement: Phase 1's in-process bus cannot survive a consumer restart, cannot replay, cannot fan out to independent consumers with independent failure domains, and cannot be scaled. Consumer lag metrics and a replay tool were deliberately not delivered because Phase 10 owns Prometheus and nothing needed replay yet."}, {"id": "development_plan_phase_3_real_market_data", "label": "Phase 3 \u2014 Real Market Data and Historical Depth", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Closed with one honest caveat: the real provider adapter has never run against the live Alpaca API because no credentials exist in this environment. It was validated by reading it against its own documented constraints, which found three defects including one that would have broken live streaming outright."}, {"id": "development_plan_phase_4_streaming_and_caching", "label": "Phase 4 \u2014 Live Streaming and Caching", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "development_plan_phase_5_authentication", "label": "Phase 5 \u2014 Authentication, Authorization, Multi-Tenancy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Placed here because the next phase is the first that stores per-user records; retrofitting ownership onto existing tables and endpoints is far more expensive and far less safe than building it before the tables exist. The hard gate is a test that user B gets 404 on user A's resource for every owner-scoped endpoint."}, {"id": "development_plan_phase_6_strategy_and_backtesting", "label": "Phase 6 \u2014 Strategy Core and Backtesting", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "development_plan_phase_7_paper_trading", "label": "Phase 7 \u2014 Paper Trading", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "development_plan_backtest_paper_consistency_test", "label": "Backtest / Paper Consistency Test", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The same strategy over the same bars must produce the same fills whether run through the backtester or the live paper path. It is the central claim of the shared-core decision and must be enforced by a test, not by inspection; the risk table names it 'the tripwire', and divergence is fixed at the simulator, never with a patch on one side."}, {"id": "development_plan_phase_8_anomaly_detection", "label": "Phase 8 \u2014 Anomaly Detection", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The ML detector must be compared against the baseline on held-out data and the comparison written down. If it does not beat the baseline, the baseline stays the default \u2014 that outcome is an acceptable result, not a failure. A grep-based test asserts no text anywhere claims detection of manipulation, fraud or financial crime."}, {"id": "development_plan_phase_9_alerts", "label": "Phase 9 \u2014 Alerts and Notifications", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "development_plan_phase_10_observability", "label": "Phase 10 \u2014 Observability and Performance Measurement", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "development_plan_phase_11_failure_recovery", "label": "Phase 11 \u2014 End-to-End and Failure-Recovery Hardening", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "development_plan_phase_12_aws_deployment", "label": "Phase 12 \u2014 AWS Deployment", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "development_plan_definition_of_done", "label": "Definition of Done (Every Phase)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A phase is done when the checklist is true, not when the feature demos: exit criteria objectively verified, migrations reversible up\u2192down\u2192up, no hard-coded value that must be configurable, no performance claim without a benchmark, no new dependency without a written justification."}, {"id": "development_plan_risk_register", "label": "Risks to Watch Across the Plan", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each risk names the signal that it is happening and the response: infrastructure sprawl, backtest/paper divergence, provider surprises, ML theatre, scope creep into a real trading system, invented metrics, and overclaiming on anomaly detection."}], "edges": [{"source": "development_plan_development_plan", "target": "architecture_tradewatch_architecture", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md", "source_location": "Companion to", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "development_plan_phase_10_observability", "target": "benchmarks_readme_benchmarks", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source":